# Overview

Cursor is the primary implementation agent for this repository, but parallel agents may also contribute changes or repository metadata.

## Coordination rules

- Assume nearby files may have been edited by another agent since the last read.
- Before making a non-trivial patch, re-open the target files and reconcile with the latest contents.
- Prefer narrow, purpose-built diffs over large rewrites, formatting sweeps, or broad file moves.
- When work overlaps, preserve user-visible behavior and document the intended coordination point in durable repo metadata if needed.
- Prefer updating shared guidance in `AGENTS.md` or `.cursor/` docs/rules instead of leaving ephemeral TODOs for other agents.

## When updating `.cursor/`

- Keep Cursor-specific workflow instructions inside `.cursor/`.
- Keep repository-wide expectations in the root `AGENTS.md`.
- Use new rules sparingly; add them only when the behavior should be reused across future sessions.
